  "claim_scope": "For every universe and arbitrary Sorts/Value/Var with the existing group instances, initial Frame and Programme, birth stopping indices are generated from the existing Type-valued CP75 receipts in the same Shared.frames history. They are StrictMono and admit Type-valued covers beyond every bound; each selected point carries the actual settled action, original canonical nextBorn and debt-admission compiler receipt. The direct gate consumes the original configured Observation full-prefix character/readout for arbitrary intermediate ticks. Its born raw-family bridge reads old frame.activeEnvironment and the actual raw-stage delta; it does not identify that raw observation with the separately decoded born.activeEnvironment.",
  "certified_machine_facts": [
    "The frozen generic Births module and source-policy direct gate independently pass fresh trust0/warningAsError; core import and pressure provenance checks also pass.",
    "Kernel actual generic core is 202 local modules, with zero domain imports. The source-policy gate graph is 213. Full inherited domain pressure union is 742; 741 dependencies are exact source/import/artifact reuse from the formal CP75 certificate, with no dependency recompile here.",
    "All 12 production declarations preserve universe u. startIndex/birthIndex read actual CP75 receipt distances and Type settlement data; no new direct future choose or future query table is constructed.",
    "startIndex0=0, birth=start+receipt.distance and nextStart=birth+1. Source-derived distance nonnegativity proves strict successor growth, StrictMono and ordinal<=birthIndex ordinal.",
    "cover returns Sigma ordinal plus PLift inequality as actual Type data; cover_after directly supplies a source index strictly beyond an arbitrary bound. No minimal-distance statement is needed or asserted.",
    "actual_action extracts the same receipt actual inl settlement. actual_next and actual_compiles directly consume CP75 original runtime nextBorn and debt-admission compilation mouths at the generated source index.",
    "covered_tick_read embeds any supplied tick in Fin(birthIndex coverOrdinal+1) and calls the existing Observation.character_source_read at offset0 over that entire prefix, including intermediate ticks. No production Observation wrapper was added.",
    "actual_birth_receipt is the original Observation.actual_source_receipt at the actual generated birth index, using the original configured runtime/readout object.",
    "born_raw_environment uses the existing nextBorn registration=frame.request, Frame.raw_environment and request_environment. observed_after_birth reads the original rawSource environment as old active; birth_stage_delta is updateInventory old.raw(active-old.raw).",
    "All 10 printed key mouths depend only on propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. The 13,166-declaration closure of the 19 audited production/direct-consumer seeds has no domain declaration owner or actor.generate dependency."
  ],
  "mouth_audit": {
    "kind": "Source-owned cofinal indexing of actual debt-admission points plus direct existing full-prefix readout consumption",
    "source_inputs": "Only the existing initial Frame, Programme and Nat ordinal/bound. No target/coverage/terminal/positive-branch witness is supplied to construct a stopping index.",
    "Type_data": "Source receipt provides Nat distance and Type settlement; cover is Sigma Nat PLift, not a mere Nonempty Disposition or existential proposition.",
    "same_actual_history": "Every index and receipt uses the same configured Shared.frames/runtime. No parallel root, new scheduler/controller or future query table is installed.",
    "readout_object": "Existing configured Observation.rawSource, character_source_read, environment_actual, stage_actual and actual_source_receipt are consumed directly.",
    "full_prefix": "The generated bound is used as the original prefix bound, with the requested intermediate tick as a Fin index; observations are not reduced to the selected birth values.",
    "raw_bridge": "nextBorn.rawRead.environment=old frame.activeEnvironment. This is the registered raw family, not a new claim about the decoder result.",
    "new_Observation_production_wrapper": false,
    "NoMagic_positive_branch": false
  },
